  "description": "Prior Approval for change of use from commercial, business and service use (Class E) to 23 x self-contained residential unit (Class C3) under Class MA",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Kings Park Ward",
  "last_updated": "2026-10-06T07:51:43.440Z",
  "street_name": "GLYN ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The applicant has failed to provide sufficient documentary evidence or annotated operational layout plans to demonstrate on the balance of probabilities that the building was in continuous, lawful Use Class E (or predecessor qualifying use classes) for a period of at least two years prior to the application date. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the criteria set out under Paragraphs MA.1(1)(b), MA.1(2)(a), and MA.1(2)(b) of Class MA, Part 3, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The applicant has failed to demonstrate that all habitable rooms of the dwellinghouses would receive adequate natural light, owing to single-aspect ground-floor layouts, shadowing from adjacent structures, and drawing discrepancies. In the absence of a BRE-compliant Daylight and Sunlight Assessment, the LPA cannot conclude otherwise, and the scheme fails to satisfy Paragraph MA.2(2)(f) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development represents a change of use to a &quot;more vulnerable&quot; residential classification within an area identified as being at risk of surface water flooding. In the absence of a site-specific Flood Risk Assessment, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development would be safe from flooding over its lifetime without increasing flood risk elsewhere, contrary to Paragraph MA.2(2)(c) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development relies upon external physical building operations, including new external bin and cycle storage structures and facade alterations (glazing and bricking up openings) to facilitate the residential use. Class MA provides permitted development rights strictly for a change of use and does not grant planning permission for physical operational development. As these works fall outside the statutory scope of Class MA, they cannot be approved under this prior approval submission, and planning permission is required.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a suitable Unilateral Undertaking or S106 securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the Controlled Parking Zone, the development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network, contrary to Local Plan policy LP45&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;and policy T6 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Furthermore, the internal cycle storage provides insufficient clearance for safe manoeuvring, and the refuse servicing requires a bin drag distance exceeding 50 metres to the highway (breaching BS 5906:2005 guidance), causing unacceptable transport impacts and failing to satisfy Paragraph MA.2(2)(a)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-185f4296-7fff-c20c-03cb-385cbb176710&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
